{"clientPlatform": "android", "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-5495e9c4-g0apvl", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": "CLAUDIA — RESTORE ALL RAINBOW AGENTS AND RUN ALL FIVE APPROVED GAME SCREENS IN PARALLEL\n\nURGENT: I AM SWITCHING CLAUDE ACCOUNTS BECAUSE MY PREVIOUS ACCOUNT RAN OUT OF USAGE CREDITS.\n\nI want to continue developing my EXISTING Rainbow Android game with multiple specialized Claude agents working simultaneously.\n\nDO NOT START A NEW GAME, REBUILD MY COMPLETED SCREENS, OR DISCARD EXISTING AGENT WORK.\n\nMy highest priority is reproducing my ORIGINAL APPROVED GAME SCREENS as closely as technically possible in real playable 3D.\n\nI want all five playable screens progressing in parallel, with Screen 08 remaining my highest priority for final approval.\n\n1. RESTORE MY EXACT GITHUB PROJECT\n\nRepository:\n\nhttps://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\n\nLead working branch:\n\n\"ccr-d4240b15-rl1i72\"\n\nExisting specialist branches:\n\nScreen 04:\n\"claude/rainbow-s04-match\"\n\nScreen 05:\n\"claude/rainbow-s05-match\"\n\nScreen 06:\n\"claude/rainbow-s06-match\"\n\nScreen 07:\n\"claude/rainbow-s07-match\"\n\nScreen 08 Benny:\n\"claude/rainbow-s08-benny08-bake\"\n\nScreen 08 camera and gameplay:\n\"claude/rainbow-s08-camclear\"\n\nPrevious recovery branch:\n\n\"ccr-9c4a8ad6-xovgsx\"\n\nVerify the newest remote commit on every branch.\n\nCheck whether agents completed additional work or saved newer checkpoints before the previous Claude account ran out of credits.\n\nDo not assume old cloud sessions or agents are still running.\n\nPreserve all earlier checkpoints.\n\nDo not automatically merge, overwrite, reset, or rebuild any existing work.\n\n2. RESTORE ALL FILES, AGENTS AND DEVELOPMENT TOOLS\n\nRestore and verify:\n\n- All 13 original approved reference images.\n- All ten existing specialist-agent definitions.\n- All Git LFS assets and generated 3D environments.\n- Blender, Three.js, Image-Blaster and Playwright.\n- Android SDK and APK build tools.\n- Camera-matching and texture-projection scripts.\n- World Labs Marble integrations and saved generation assets.\n- fal.ai integration and existing edited scenery.\n- Existing MCP servers, plugins and configurations where supported.\n- All screen-specific QA results and comparison images.\n- Project instructions, handoffs, scripts and autosave settings.\n\nRead:\n\n\"CLAUDE.md\"\n\n\"docs/NEW_CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_HANDOFF.md\"\n\n\"docs/PARALLEL_PROGRESS.md\"\n\n\"qa/match/08/NOTES.md\"\n\n\"docs/FLOW_VIDEO.md\"\n\nRead each specialist's existing status and notes before resuming development.\n\nPreserve the original approved images unchanged.\n\n3. ENABLE REAL PARALLEL AGENT DEVELOPMENT\n\nTHIS IS THE MOST IMPORTANT PART OF MY REQUEST.\n\nCheck the parallel development capabilities available in this Claude account.\n\nI want multiple agents working SIMULTANEOUSLY, not merely assigned tasks that all wait for one agent to finish.\n\nUse supported Claude Code cloud sessions, isolated Git worktrees, subagents or agent teams, whichever provides the most reliable parallel execution.\n\nIf the experimental agent-teams feature is available and appropriate, check whether the following setting is required:\n\n\"CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1\"\n\nConfigure it securely where supported.\n\nHowever, do not let the absence of experimental agent teams prevent parallel work. Separate Claude Code cloud sessions are also acceptable.\n\nEach agent must have its own working environment and Git branch.\n\nDO NOT CLAIM MULTIPLE AGENTS ARE RUNNING UNTIL THEIR SESSIONS ARE ACTUALLY STARTED AND VERIFIED.\n\n4. ASSIGN THE SCREEN SPECIALISTS\n\nLEAD CLAUDIA — PROJECT COORDINATOR\n\nCoordinate every screen, protect shared files, verify GitHub backups, monitor progress, and manage integration.\n\nSCREEN 08 — BENNY SPECIALIST\n\nContinue the latest Benny improvements, including fur shading, knitted beanie, pom-pom, star, approved colors, and water splash.\n\nPreserve the existing Screen 08 scenery reconstruction.\n\nSCREEN 08 — CAMERA SPECIALIST\n\nContinue the recorded gameplay-video investigation, camera obstruction fixes, transition improvements, and moving-camera tests.\n\nSCREEN 04 AGENT\n\nResume the existing Screen 04 reconstruction.\n\nPrevious reports showed approximately 97.6% scenery matching in the approved-camera test.\n\nCorrect the smeared gold tunnel surfaces, mirrored water textures, and moving-camera distortions.\n\nAn additional single targeted fal.ai environment-only edit was previously authorized. Check whether it has already run before spending anything.\n\nSCREEN 05 AGENT\n\nResume the existing Screen 05 work.\n\nPrevious reports showed approximately 93.3% scenery matching and 96.5% water matching.\n\nPreserve the improved water around Benny.\n\nCorrect the 100-versus-91-coin discrepancy and remaining scenery differences.\n\nSCREEN 06 AGENT\n\nResume the previously started Screen 06 work from its latest saved GitHub checkpoint.\n\nRecreate the original approved scenery with accurate real 3D geometry, colors, lighting, and water.\n\nSCREEN 07 AGENT\n\nResume the previously started Screen 07 work.\n\nPreserve its connection and gameplay transition into Screen 08.\n\nReconstruct its approved scenery with the same high-fidelity method.\n\nQUALITY-CONTROL SPECIALISTS\n\nUse the remaining available design, geometry, camera, lighting, testing, and visual-comparison agents to support these workstreams.\n\n5. RUN THE WORKSTREAMS AT THE SAME TIME\n\nI want the following screens actively progressing:\n\n- Screen 04\n- Screen 05\n- Screen 06\n- Screen 07\n- Screen 08\n\nKeep the two Screen 08 specialists coordinated under Lead Claudia.\n\nIf available usage limits or hardware resources cannot safely support all workstreams concurrently, run the maximum safe number and tell me which ones are active and which are queued.\n\nPrioritize protecting Screen 08, but do not unnecessarily delay the other screens.\n\nDo not launch duplicate agents for work already active.\n\nDo not run several agents that overwrite the same shared files.\n\n6. KEEP EVERY WORKSTREAM ISOLATED\n\nEach specialist must save to its own existing branch or a clearly identified continuation branch.\n\nProtect shared Benny files, HUD, gameplay systems, cameras and approved reference assets.\n\nOnly the lead coordinator may authorize shared-code integration after checking for conflicts.\n\nDo not merge unfinished work into the previous project branch.\n\nKeep all successful work recoverable.\n\nMaintain a clear development status for every screen.\n\n7. MAINTAIN MAXIMUM VISUAL ACCURACY\n\nMy ORIGINAL APPROVED SCREENS are the source of truth.\n\nFor each playable environment, match:\n\n- Exact scenery and backgrounds.\n- Camera framing and perspective.\n- Washing-machine architecture.\n- Metallic materials and gold rings.\n- Blue and pink water formations.\n- Foam, bubbles and water splashes.\n- Colors, lighting, highlights and reflections.\n- Benny's appearance and position.\n- Collectible coins and gameplay HUD.\n- Real 3D movement and steering.\n\nUse the successful camera-matching, artwork projection and fitted-3D-geometry methods developed for Screen 08.\n\nDo not use World Labs Marble to invent replacement scenery when the existing reconstruction method produces more faithful results.\n\n8. RESTORE WORLD LABS MARBLE AND FAL.AI\n\nReuse my existing World Labs Marble and fal.ai accounts.\n\nThe last reported World Labs balance was approximately 5,420 credits.\n\nI previously purchased $10 in fal.ai credits, and some were used for earlier edits.\n\nDo not create replacement accounts.\n\nIf the existing secure API connections are already functional, verify and reuse them.\n\nOtherwise, request the same credentials through secure secrets forms.\n\nNever expose API keys in chat or commit them to GitHub.\n\nRestore the existing Image-Blaster workflow, Marble assets, and previously completed fal.ai edits.\n\nDo not repeat successful paid generations.\n\nDo not purchase additional credits or enable automatic top-ups.\n\n9. TEST ACTUAL ANDROID GAMEPLAY\n\nEach agent must validate the approved checkpoint and moving-camera views.\n\nCheck camera obstructions, texture stretching, steering, transitions, collisions, coin collection, and character movement.\n\nPreserve the intended 91 coins and reward behavior.\n\nDo not change gameplay mechanics just to obtain a better screenshot.\n\nProduce Android test builds when the appropriate changes are ready.\n\nShow the approved original and the new actual 3D game rendering separately at full size.\n\nA high fixed-camera pixel score alone does not mean the entire moving 3D environment is approved.\n\n10. PROTECT MY GOOGLE FLOW VIDEO PLAN\n\nThe cartoon-girl opening and ending scenes are Google Flow videos.\n\nThey are not playable 3D environments.\n\nPreserve \"docs/FLOW_VIDEO.md\" and the existing game-video handoff.\n\nDo not spend time rebuilding the cinematic scenes as gameplay levels.\n\nPreserve all 13 approved reference images and keep every one's production role documented.\n\n11. SAVE EVERYTHING AUTOMATICALLY\n\nRestore the existing five-minute GitHub autosave workflow where supported.\n\nEach agent must commit and push completed work to its own branch.\n\nVerify remote GitHub commits and Git LFS storage.\n\nMaintain:\n\n\"docs/PARALLEL_PROGRESS.md\"\n\nRecord for every screen:\n\n- Assigned specialist.\n- Working branch.\n- Running-session status.\n- Latest verified commit.\n- Completed improvements.\n- Latest visual measurements.\n- Unfinished problems.\n- Test results.\n- Next task.\n- Approval status.\n\nDo not confuse saved work with actively running agents.\n\n12. GIVE ME A PARALLEL-AGENT STATUS REPORT\n\nBefore claiming restoration is complete, tell me:\n\n1. Whether the correct lead branch was restored.\n2. The latest verified commit on each specialist branch.\n3. Whether all 13 original images are unchanged.\n4. Whether all ten agent definitions are restored.\n5. Whether World Labs and fal.ai are connected.\n6. Which parallel-work features are available and enabled.\n7. Which screen sessions are actually running right now.\n8. Whether every agent has its own isolated workspace.\n9. Which screens have outstanding visual problems.\n10. Whether all active sessions are saving successfully to GitHub.\n\nIf something is missing, identify the blocker and a safe recovery plan.\n\nFINAL INSTRUCTIONS\n\nI WANT ALL FIVE PLAYABLE SCREENS WORKED ON IN PARALLEL, WITHOUT LOSING VISUAL ACCURACY.\n\nDo not restart existing completed work.\n\nDo not abandon Screen 08.\n\nDo not redesign the approved artwork.\n\nDo not overwrite another agent's branch.\n\nDo not integrate unfinished work without review.\n\nDo not mark a screen fully approved until I personally approve it.\n\nSTART BY VERIFYING \"ccr-d4240b15-rl1i72\" AND ALL SIX SPECIALIST BRANCHES, RESTORING THEIR LATEST WORK, AND LAUNCHING THE MAXIMUM SAFE NUMBER OF PARALLEL SCREEN-DEVELOPMENT SESSIONS.\n\nMy goal is to finish ALL my original approved gameplay screens as faithfully as technically possible, while using my other Claude account's available credits efficiently.", "role": "user"}, "origin": {"kind": "human"}, "parentUuid": "5cca777d-3cac-49f4-9f8c-16341566ed62", "permissionMode": "default", "promptId": "3c2649a1-3936-408a-9c05-4d6a6d8a1714", "promptSource": "sdk", "sessionId": "1577e4f2-096c-5327-af57-8fe315cad85a", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T16:26:26.864Z", "turnAttributionKey": "7fd5c042-52de-4575-b209-00b0dbf71d1c", "turnOrigin": "human", "turnPosition": {"promptIndex": 1, "turnIndex": 1}, "type": "user", "userType": "external", "uuid": "7fd5c042-52de-4575-b209-00b0dbf71d1c", "version": "2.1.326"}
